# Served Teach App — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` for local tooling/tests, and to `.dev.vars` for `wrangler dev`
# (both are gitignored). In production, set the worker-runtime values as
# Wrangler secrets (`wrangler secret put NAME`) and bind R2 in wrangler.toml —
# do NOT ship real secrets in this file.
#
# Nothing here is required by the current test suite (the pure modules + the
# in-memory Hub adapter need no environment). These become live with slice 0.

# --- Neon (the Hub) ---------------------------------------------------------
# Pooled Postgres connection string the worker uses at runtime (ADR-0002/0005).
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST.neon.tech/DBNAME?sslmode=require"
# A Neon *test branch* URL — the Neon HubRepository adapter's contract tests
# (src/hub/repository.test.ts) run against this, never against production.
DATABASE_URL_TEST="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@TEST-BRANCH-HOST.neon.tech/DBNAME?sslmode=require"

# --- Cloudflare account / tooling (publish + deploy) ------------------------
# Used by wrangler (and the Neon/Cloudflare MCP) to publish blobs and deploy.
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID="your-cloudflare-account-id"
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN="scoped-token-with-workers-and-r2-permissions"

# --- R2 (the Artifact store) ------------------------------------------------
# Bucket holding Lesson/Reference HTML blobs. The bucket itself is bound in
# wrangler.toml (an R2 binding) and served only through the worker, never
# publicly (ADR-0005). The name is here so the publish shell knows the target.
R2_BUCKET_NAME="served-teach-artifacts"

# --- Cloudflare Access (auth gate) ------------------------------------------
# v1 gates the whole app via Cloudflare Access (ADR-0004). The worker verifies
# the Access JWT against your team domain + application audience (AUD) tag.
CF_ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN="your-team.cloudflareaccess.com"
CF_ACCESS_AUD="application-audience-tag-from-the-access-policy"
